# The verdict {isGroup: true}

[Turn to Pragmatic Genealogy sometimes]: Philosophers should turn to Pragmatic Genealogy sometimes, for certain goals.
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 383", source: "\"Should philosophers turn to Pragmatic Genealogy? Sometimes, for certain goals.\"", note: "ONE OF TWO CONTENTIONS. The paper answers its own title question here, and then, in its last paragraph, argues a further point about the worldview behind the method. Joining the two would assert a single thesis the paper never states; dropping either loses half its work."}

[The method has certain limits]: The objections raised against Queloz's discussion show only that Pragmatic Genealogy has certain limits.
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 383", source: "\"They only show that it has certain limits\"", note: "Not an apex. The paper uses this claim once more, as evidence that something is wrong with the Weltanschauung — so it is an intermediate conclusion, and the last paragraph is where the paper stops."}

[The method is not useless]: The objections raised, even if sound, do not show that Pragmatic Genealogy is useless. #conceded
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 383", source: "\"these objections, even if sound, do not show the method is useless\""}

