# The worldview behind the method {isGroup: true}

[The Weltanschauung]: We should not submit ourselves to the definitions of the concepts we have but rather construct those concepts for ourselves on the basis of our needs and wants. #reported
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "pp. 372, 383", source: "\"We should not submit ourselves to the definitions of the concepts we have but rather construct those concepts for ourselves on the basis of our needs and wants\"", note: "The paper states this view twice, eleven pages apart. Quoted here from p. 372, where the three motivations converge on it; the conclusion on p. 383 puts it again as a slogan about concepts being made for us, and that is the form the last argument turns against. An elision joining the two would bridge most of the paper, so only the first is quoted."}

[The engineering Weltanschauung is constraining]: The Weltanschauung behind Pragmatic Genealogy is supposed to be liberating, but to Prescott-Couch it feels constraining.
