# What Pragmatic Genealogy is, and what motivates it {isGroup: true}

[The Pragmatic Question replaces the Socratic]: Pragmatic Genealogists recommend that, in understanding important concepts, we orient our inquiry around the Pragmatic Question — what is the point or purpose of our possessing the concept X? — rather than around the Socratic Question, 'What is X?'. #reported
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 368", source: "\"we should instead orient our inquiry around the Pragmatic Question: what is the point or purpose of our possessing the concept X?\""}

[Genealogies are state-of-nature models]: Genealogies, in Queloz's reconstruction, are idealized state-of-nature models that serve to help us understand the functions served by various conceptual practices. #reported
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 368", source: "\"idealized state-of-nature models that serve to help us understand the functions served by various conceptual practices\""}

[Craig reverse-engineers knowledge]: Craig's genealogy reverse-engineers the function of our concept of knowledge, which is identifying good informants. #reported
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 369", source: "\"Craig's genealogy 'reverse-engineers' the 'function' of our concept of knowledge (identifying good informants)\""}

[Genealogies are state-of-nature models]
    <+ [Craig reverse-engineers knowledge]

