    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 371", source: "\"the Pragmatic Question is sometimes motivated by a substantive axiological thesis: that what is ultimately valuable is 'practical'\"", note: "The quotation stops at the footnote marker that interrupts the sentence; `rather than, say, epistemic` is the parenthesis that follows it."}
(3) [The methodological motivation]: The Pragmatic Question is sometimes motivated by a methodological thesis: we can get insight into how we should change our practices by seeing where they came from and what holds them in place.
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 371", source: "\"the Pragmatic Question is sometimes motivated by a methodological thesis: we can get insight into how we should change our practices by seeing where they came from and what holds them in place\""}
(4) [The commitments interconnect]: The commitments are loosely interconnected into a broad Weltanschauung.
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 372", source: "\"the commitments are loosely interconnected into a broad Weltanschauung\""}
