## What the three challenges license

<The case for a modest role>: Functional considerations are entangled with other theoretical questions and can smuggle substantive commitments in as method, so they belong among the other considerations rather than above them.
    {fidelity: "compression", pinpoint: "p. 375", note: "CONDUCTIVE. The three challenges are convergent — each stands if the others fail — and the author's own concession that the interweaving does not show the Pragmatic Question misguided is weighed in as part of the argument, not treated as an objection to it."}

<The case for a modest role>

(1) [Socratic Questioning already includes Pragmatic Questioning]
(2) [Answering Pragmatic Questions often requires Socratic answers]
(3) [The Pragmatic Question misses the key issue]
(4) [Interconnection does not show the Pragmatic Question misguided]: Noting that Socratic and Pragmatic questioning can be interconnected does not show that asking the Pragmatic Question is misguided. #conceded
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 375", source: "\"Noting that Socratic and Pragmatic questioning can be interconnected does not show that asking the Pragmatic Question is misguided\""}
(5) [Functional considerations may still be useful]: Considerations about the basic needs served by conceptual practices may be useful to consider when it comes to most philosophical questions. #conceded
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 375", source: "\"considerations about the basic needs served by conceptual practices may be useful to consider, but I see little reason to give exclusive weight to functional considerations or to give them some superordinary role\"", note: "The quotation runs on into the author's own `but`, which is drawn separately as the next step of this argument. Cutting it off would make a concession look like an endorsement."}
(6) [Functional considerations are interconnected with other issues]: In many cases the relevant functional considerations are interconnected with other theoretical issues.
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 375", source: "\"in many cases, the relevant functional considerations are interconnected with other theoretical issues\""}
(7) [Starting with functionality can beg questions]: Starting with functionality can be a way of begging substantive questions through the guise of methodology.
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 375", source: "\"starting with functionality can be a way of begging substantive questions through the guise of methodology\""}
-----
(8) [No exclusive weight to functional considerations]: There is little reason to give exclusive weight to functional considerations or to give them some superordinary role.
    {fidelity: "paraphrase", pinpoint: "p. 375", source: "\"I see little reason to give exclusive weight to functional considerations or to give them some superordinary role\""}

[Functional considerations deserve only a modest role]: It is better to take the more modest approach of considering functional claims within the context of other complementary and competing considerations, in the way that typical Socratic exchange unfolds.
    {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 375", source: "\"It is better to take the more modest approach of considering functional claims within the context of other complementary and competing considerations, in the way that typical Socratic exchange unfolds.\"", note: "The positive counterpart of the claim above it, in the author's next sentence: no exclusive weight, therefore a place among the other considerations. Drawn as a claim that one supports rather than as a further inference."}
    <+ [No exclusive weight to functional considerations]

[Functional considerations deserve only a modest role]
    +> [The method has certain limits]

